# Keys given to a tutorial note (see tutwin.c, tutwin_note.scene). A letter does nothing to a note; Return and Space close it (the
# popup answers its default button). For a mode 0 note the window's own key handler declines (the note's mode is 0), for the others
# (here mode 2, with the Continue and End Tour buttons) it takes the note down and keeps the key. A mode 1 note (the farm's, which
# shows a picture) hands the key that closed it to the console after the note, and goes on to the tour if its button asks.
25 load
26 state tw_fields 0x8cc1e4 0x5c
26 state tw_flags 0x8cc244 8
26 state tw_seen 0x9a64ac 0x14
26 state tw_draw 0x8c9fd0 4
44 open tut_terrain
50 snap mode0
52 key a
56 snap mode0-letter
58 key Return
62 snap mode0-return
64 open tut_terrain_m2
70 snap mode2
72 key a
76 snap mode2-letter
78 key space
82 snap mode2-space
84 open tut_terrain_m2
90 snap mode2-again
92 key Return
96 snap mode2-return
98 open tut_picture
104 snap picture
106 key Return
112 snap picture-return
114 open tut_picture
120 snap picture-2
122 key F2                 # taken by the note, which hands it on to the console: the lab summary opens
128 snap picture-f2
130 click 636 520          # its Close
134 snap picture-f2-closed
136 close
# The base screen can open under the notes (Return reaches the game too): its leader portraits (and a pixel at the left panel's corner) animate slower than a snap's burst.
mask 265 625 310 680
mask 700 625 760 680
mask 134 709 138 713
